.TH AIZER 1 "2026-11-08" "aizer-VERSION"
.SH NAME
aizer \- minimal Wayland application launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aizer
.SH DESCRIPTION
aizer is a minimal application launcher for Wayland. It shows a centered
rectangle, reads the list of applications, filters it as you type, and
launches the selected entry. It draws nothing except the widget and its
text, and has no bar, no icons and no history.
.P
aizer is configured at compile time only. There is no configuration file,
no IPC and no reload mechanism. See
.BR CONFIGURATION .
.P
aizer does not start other programs by itself. Bind it to a key in the
compositor.
.SH OPTIONS
aizer takes no options. Any argument prints a usage message to standard
error and exits.
.SH USAGE
Run
.B aizer
from a key binding. A centered widget appears, the application list is
loaded, and the launcher waits for input.
.P
Type to filter the list. Matching is case-insensitive and works on the
application name and its generic name, as a substring or a subsequence.
.P
.TP
.B Up, Down
Move the selection.
.TP
.B Enter
Launch the selected application, or a typed command line with arguments
such as
.IR "alacritty -e htop" .
The launcher closes after a successful launch.
.TP
.B Esc
Close without launching.
.TP
.B Backspace
Delete the last character.
.P
Held arrow keys repeat after a short delay.
.P
The widget closes itself after a successful launch, so it does not stay
in the background.
.SH CONFIGURATION
aizer is configured by editing
.I aizer.h
and recompiling:
.P
.RS
.EX
$ $EDITOR aizer.h
$ make clean install
.EE
.RE
.P
Then restart aizer. The most important options are:
.TP
.B WIDGET_W, WIDGET_H
Widget size in pixels.
.TP
.B ROW_H, MAX_ROWS
Row height and number of visible rows.
.TP
.B COLOR_*
Colors in
.B 0xRRGGBBAA
format.
.TP
.B BG_ALPHA
Background alpha of the widget surface.
.TP
.B FONT_NAME, FONT_SIZE, ROW_FONT_SIZE
Font family and sizes, resolved through fontconfig.
.TP
.B PROMPT
Text shown before the query.
.TP
.B QUERY_MAX
Size of the query buffer in bytes.
.TP
.B BLINK_MS
Cursor blink half period in milliseconds.
.TP
.B REPEAT_DELAY
Delay before key repeat starts, in milliseconds.
.TP
.B LIST_PATH_EXEC
Set to 1 to list executables from
.BR $PATH .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The Wayland display to connect to.
.SH EXIT STATUS
aizer exits with 0 when it closes normally (Esc or after a launch). It
exits with a non-zero status if it cannot connect to the Wayland display
or on a fatal error.
.SH STANDARDS
aizer uses the Wayland core protocol, the wlr layer shell extension, and
xkbcommon for keyboard input. It runs under any Wayland compositor that
supports those.
.SH BUGS AND LIMITATIONS
.IP \(bu 2
aizer shows no icons, images or logos. The list is text only.
.IP \(bu 2
aizer keeps no history and no state between runs.
.IP \(bu 2
aizer is a single widget on a single output. It does not manage windows.
.IP \(bu 2
The application list is read at startup. Changes to
.B .desktop
files are picked up on the next run.
.IP \(bu 2
aizer does not run under X11.
.P
Report bugs at the project issue tracker.
